{#- The earnings slider panel and the ladder table, two sibling blocks. Include once per page, inside an element
    marked [data-earnings-slider] that lays them out (index.njk stacks them, pricing.njk puts them side by side).
    Optional, set before the include: `sliderTableWhere` (where the table sits, default "below") and `sliderNote`
    (a last line in the panel). main.js reads the ladder from tr[data-price]. -#}
{%- set first = ladder.brackets[0] -%}
<div class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 ring-1 ring-black/10">
  {#- Fixed-height slot: the no-JS note and the controls swap in place, so nothing shifts. -#}
  <div class="min-h-37">
    <p class="text-sm text-muted" data-slider-fallback>Every bracket is in the table {{ sliderTableWhere or "below" }}. With JavaScript on, a slider picks one.</p>
    <div data-slider-controls hidden>
      <label for="earnings-range" class="block font-medium text-ink">Creator's monthly earnings</label>
      <input id="earnings-range" class="mt-2 block h-11 w-full cursor-pointer" type="range" min="0" max="{{ ladder.brackets.length - 1 }}" step="1" value="0" aria-valuetext="{{ first.label }}" data-slider-range />
      <div class="flex justify-between text-xs text-muted" aria-hidden="true"><span>{{ first.label }}</span><span>{{ (ladder.brackets | last).label }}</span></div>
      <div class="mt-3 flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
        <label for="earnings-count" class="font-medium text-ink">Number of creators</label>
        <input id="earnings-count" class="h-11 w-24 rounded-xl border border-black/20 bg-white px-3 text-ink tabular-nums" type="number" min="1" max="500" step="1" value="10" inputmode="numeric" data-slider-count />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-6 border-t border-line pt-6 text-ink tabular-nums">
    <p class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight" data-out="bracket">{{ first.label }}</p>
    <p class="mt-3">Infloww: <strong data-out="price">${{ first.inflowwPrice }}</strong> per creator per month</p>
    <p class="mt-1">Inflowwww: <strong>${{ first.ours }}</strong></p>
    {#- The long sentence is not live; main.js writes a short line with the price into the sr-only region below. -#}
    <p class="mt-3 min-h-18">At <span data-out="count">10</span> <span data-out="noun">creators</span> in this bracket, 12 months at Infloww's list price come to <strong data-out="year">${{ (first.inflowwPrice * 12 * 10) | round | string | replace(r/\B(?=(\d{3})+(?!\d))/g, ",") }}</strong>. On ours you pay for the server and any proxies, plus someone's time.</p>
    <p class="sr-only" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" data-out="live"></p>
  </div>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">This assumes every creator sits in the same bracket. If yours don't, add up their rows in the table.</p>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">With one or two creators, the yearly saving can be smaller than paying someone to set up and look after a server. Count that before you switch.</p>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">Source: <a class="text-link" href="{{ ladder.source }}">{{ ladder.sourceLabel }}</a>, captured <span class="whitespace-nowrap">{{ site.captureDate }}</span>. List prices.</p>
  {%- if sliderNote %}
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm font-medium text-ink">{{ sliderNote }}</p>
  {%- endif %}
</div>
<div>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl bg-white ring-1 ring-black/10">
    <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
      <caption class="px-4 pt-4 pb-2 text-left text-ink">
        Infloww for OnlyFans: monthly price per creator profile, by the creator's monthly earnings ({{ ladder.sourceLabel }}, captured <span class="whitespace-nowrap">{{ site.captureDate }}</span>). Their Fansly card uses the same slider; the pricing page's code holds one price table.
      </caption>
      <thead class="bg-band text-ink">
        <tr>
          <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2 font-medium max-sm:px-2.5">Creator's monthly earnings</th>
          <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2 font-medium max-sm:px-2.5">Infloww</th>
          <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2 font-medium max-sm:px-2.5">Inflowwww</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y divide-line text-ink tabular-nums">
        {%- for row in ladder.brackets %}
        <tr class="data-active:bg-cream" data-price="{{ row.inflowwPrice }}" data-label="{{ row.label }}"{{ " data-active" if loop.first }}>
          <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-2 font-normal max-sm:px-2.5">{{ row.label }}</th>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 max-sm:px-2.5">${{ row.inflowwPrice }}</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 max-sm:px-2.5"><span class="chip-free">${{ row.ours }}</span></td>
        </tr>
        {%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-muted">
    <li><strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Infloww for mym:</strong> “Starting at just $50”, per creator profile, monthly, flat (no earnings slider).</li>
    <li><strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Infloww for Fanvue:</strong> “Starting at just $50”, flat, “Monthly pricing per creator profile until 30 June 2026”. The page does not say what it costs after that date.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">
    Source: {{ ladder.sourceLabel }}, captured <span class="whitespace-nowrap">{{ site.captureDate }}</span>. Prices per creator profile per month, billed monthly.
    Inflowwww has no mym or Fanvue client.
  </p>
</div>
